<% connector_url = "#{WentHiking.public_base_url.to_s.sub(%r{/+\z}, "")}/mcp" %>

<section class="narrow">
  <p class="kicker">Connect an assistant</p>
  <h1>Post your hikes by chatting.</h1>
  <p>
    Went Hiking connects to Claude and ChatGPT, so you can post a trip the way
    you'd tell a friend about it &mdash; from the trailhead parking lot, on the
    drive home, wherever. Say something like <em>&ldquo;post my trip to the
    Goat Rocks to Went Hiking&rdquo;</em> and your assistant will interview you
    about the trip, draft the report in your voice, hand you a link to add
    photos from your camera roll, and publish only when you say it's ready.
  </p>

  <h2>Set it up with Claude</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="https://claude.ai/settings/connectors" target="_blank" rel="noopener">claude.ai &rarr; Settings &rarr; Connectors</a>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>Add custom connector</strong> and paste in <code><%= h(connector_url) %></code>.</li>
    <li>When Claude asks to connect, log in with your Went Hiking account and approve access.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Once added on the web, the connector follows you to the Claude apps on
    iPhone, Android, and desktop automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>Set it up with ChatGPT</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open ChatGPT &rarr; <strong>Settings &rarr; Apps &amp; Connectors</strong>. If you don't see an option to add one, enable developer mode under <strong>Advanced settings</strong> first.</li>
    <li>Add a new connector with the URL <code><%= h(connector_url) %></code>.</li>
    <li>Log in with your Went Hiking account when prompted and approve access.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Things worth knowing</h2>
  <p>
    Everything starts as a private draft &mdash; nothing goes public and nobody
    gets emailed until you explicitly tell your assistant to publish. Your
    assistant can only touch your own hikes, and only with the permissions you
    approve on the consent screen. Photos never pass through the assistant:
    the upload link opens right here on Went Hiking and the photos go straight
    to your trip.
  </p>
  <p>
    Questions, or something acting weird?
    <a href="mailto:kaiuhl+wenthiking@gmail.com">Send feedback</a>.
  </p>
</section>
